> tl;dr
>
> - Standardized a 15‑site UNDRR Drupal 10 ecosystem, cutting load times by 50–70% and reducing Azure spend by 20%.
> - Doubled Lighthouse SEO scores and increased campaign engagement by ~40% (e.g., GAR2025).
> - Achieved by leading a cross‑functional team and aligning engineering, editorial, and design toward shared outcomes.

We operate a multi‑domain ecosystem serving policymakers, practitioners, and the public. That means a tidy “site redesign” isn’t enough; the platform has to be fast, reliable, and readable by both humans and machines. When we kicked off this work, we framed success in terms stakeholders care about: measurable speed, lower infrastructure spend, and clearer routes for AI‑ready publishing.

What follows isn’t a heroics story; it’s the result of standardization and patience. We focused on a few high‑leverage improvements (image pipelines, caching, structured metadata, shared components) and applied them consistently across 15 sites. The compounding effect is what moved the needle.

## Problem

Critical content for decision‑makers was slowed by inconsistent theming, fragmented governance, and limited AI‑readiness. Pages were heavy, image pipelines inconsistent, and analytics lacked dimensions for segment‑level reporting.

## Approach

- Platform standardization on Drupal 10 with hybrid headless patterns.
- Performance engineering: caching strategy, image pipelines, render path audits, CWV fixes.
- AI‑readiness: RDF/SKOS metadata, JSON‑LD exports, machine‑actionable content models.
- Design‑system patterns and component theming to unify UX across 15 sites.
- Analytics: GA4 with custom dimensions; Looker Studio dashboards; chatbot referral tracking.

## Key decisions

- Consolidated asset handling; deterministic responsive images in build.
- Tightened Azure resources; tuned database and CDN caching.
- Introduced governance playbooks to harden editorial workflows.

## Outcomes

- 50–70% faster loads; 20% quarterly Azure cost reduction.
- Doubled Lighthouse SEO scores on representative pages.
- +40% campaign engagement lift (GAR2025); clearer segment insights.

